00:00:03.189 --> 00:00:05.190 align:start position:0%
october is breast cancer awareness month  and in honor of this very important  month we're catching up with an  inspirational breast cancer survivor who  is very near and dear to us we met  cheryl kolberg last season when she was  planning something special for her 50th  birthday to support finding a cure  here's an update on what she's been up  to since and what she's planning for  breast cancer awareness month this year  this woman is truly one of my heroes  she's just incredible please take a look  hey drew it's sheryl kohlberg thanks for  having me back this year i just wanted  to give you an update in  2018 i was diagnosed with breast cancer  i was in treatment for 15 months it was  very difficult but i made it through and  i've been cancer-free for almost two  years now for me running has always been  a part of my life and now that i'm  cancer-free the journey back to health  one of the things that was really  important for me was to get back into  running again  so last year it was my 50th birthday i  wanted to do something very special to  celebrate i  met people from all 50 states and ran  virtually with someone from each state  every day for 50 days over zoo i've met  so many amazing people through this  process some women who  literally have told me that because they  saw me on the show  they went and got their mammogram and  they found out they had breast cancer  they got it detected early enough and  they're fine thanks to wonderful  supporters like you drew and  bank of america i was able to raise more  than a hundred thousand dollars  for susan g komen to hopefully put a  cure to breast cancer  this year i'm doing something different  i'm running a 5k every day in october  and i'm encouraging people to join me  where they are they can run bike swim  and  take a photo of what you're doing post  it to your social media and mention at  55o for the cure i want to give hope to  women who are currently  in treatment and let them know that  someday soon they'll be in my shoes out  running again or doing whatever they  love to do i encourage everyone to get  involved and raising awareness for  breast cancer  together one mile at a time  we are so inspired by you cheryl and we  are rooting for you always don't forget  to get your mammograms and visit the 50  forthcured.org to join cheryl or to  learn more  [Music]
 

